cinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  02 MAY 95 at 15 12 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm piece of fibroadipose tissue with needle localization  and accompanied by roentgenogram  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a variegated  firm  gritty  tan pink nodule  1 1cm in greatest dimension  located 5mm from the end of the localizing wire  and abutting the inked surface  A representative section of the nodule is frozen as frozen section  1  and saved frozen  The remainder of the breast is submitted in A through F  with the nodule predominantly in A through C  Resident  JAMES J  TIESINGA  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  RIGHT BREAST  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  EDWIN S  MONUKI  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Andrew Eric Rosenberg  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Michael Ned Margolies  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST   report_end  , Absent.
